      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "The problem with this is that its intended to allow you to be handling a signal after(as) you shut down the safe signal handler. The trouble is - thats really NOT safe!!!! (consider when we continue - and is handler itself OK running afte rmain)? What about rest of the SingnalHandler code?",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Instead, use a direct pointer.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "And either REQUIRE that all safe signal handlers are removed from teh safe signal handler object before exiting, or documenting that we do that automaitcally.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
